<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn about MushroomScope and our mission to make mushroom knowledge clear, useful, and responsible."><div class="shell py-8"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'About'}]} /></div><article class="shell max-w-4xl py-12"><p class="eyebrow">Our mission</p><h1 class="mt-4 font-serif text-5xl sm:text-6xl">A clearer view of the fungal world</h1><div class="prose mt-8"><p>MushroomScope is an independent English-language knowledge project for mushroom enthusiasts, growers, nature lovers, cooks, and curious readers worldwide.</p><h2>How we work</h2><p>Our goal is to publish approachable, carefully structured references that separate established knowledge from emerging evidence. Identification content always emphasizes local expertise and conservative safety practices.</p><h2>Editorial standards</h2><p>Articles are designed to cite credible sources, show review dates, disclose limitations, and avoid medical or identification certainty where it is not justified. Read our full <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer/">safety disclaimer</a>.</p><h2>Explore MushroomScope</h2><p>Start with the <a href="/mushrooms/">mushroom encyclopedia</a>, learn a safety-first approach in <a href="/identification/">identification guides</a>, or explore practical sections about <a href="/growing/">cultivation</a>, <a href="/health/">health research</a>, and <a href="/recipes/">cooking</a>.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>
